e it and it would still be a  better option than to have your student  pushing keys on a tablet part of the  literacy essentials curriculum that  orton-gillingham see it say it here at  Wright it is so important for young  students as they're learning to read and  write so please include that as you're  working with students on home at home so  just to kind of go over some ideas stay  within the curriculum work on the sounds  and not on memorizing think about where  your words are going to come from maybe  from the old an old spelling sheet or  maybe from reading material that the  student has don't forget the importance  of putting pencil to paper it could also  be a dry erase board on a dry erase  marker on a whiteboard another good way  to get them writing and then have  students read everything to you that  they write so all of their sentences  that they've created all of their words  that they've pulled down that they've  unscrambled that they've decoded give  them the opportunity to read out loud to  you I hope you find some of these ideas  helpful as you're working at home and we  are here to answer any questions and to  offer more ideas if you need them thank  you  you
 

